{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789824370304,"sessionID":"ses_f462b66afffeUYg2nY8b6hqAEy","part":{"partID":"prt_0b9d8843d0014xwk4uUoiZB4Ea","sessionID":"ses_f462b66afffeUYg2nY8b6hqAEy","messageID":"msg_0b9d87ae6001APtS4rCpO3I7qk","type":"tool","id":"call_00_MDMKNi7T1qFMAuwf4Ogf4319","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /home/uctpiaj/work/work_tmp && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json, re\ndata=json.load(open('pages.json'))\n# locate Simpson page\nfor d in data:\n    for j,t in enumerate(d['paras']):\n        if 'Simpson' in t or 'Cravath' in t:\n            print(\"SIMPSON CTX page\", d['page'], \"idx\", j, \":\", t[:1500])\n            print()\n# page 34 paragraphs\nfor d in data:\n    if d['page']=='34':\n        for j,t in enumerate(d['paras']):\n            print(f\"[34.{j}] {t[:800]}\")\n            print()\nEOF"},"output":"SIMPSON CTX page None idx 7 : Simpson Thacher and Bartlett LLP 425 Lexington Avenue New York, NY 10017 Facsimile: (212) 455-2502 Email: rsymons@stblaw.com Attention: Ryerson Symons\n\n[34.0] TABLE OF CONTENTS\n\n[34.1] 2005 – 2007 Transactions\n\n[34.2] Target\n\n[34.3] Buyer\n\n[34.4] Announcement Date\n\n[34.5] Claire’s Stores, Inc.\n\n[34.6] Apollo Management, L.P.\n\n[34.7] March 2007\n\n[34.8] Dollar General Corporation\n\n[34.9] Kohlberg Kravis Roberts & Co. L.P.\n\n[34.10] March 2007\n\n[34.11] GNC Parent Corporation\n\n[34.12] Ares Management LLC\n\n[34.13] February 2007\n\n[34.14] Guitar Center Inc.\n\n[34.15] Bain Capital Partners, LLC\n\n[34.16] June 2007\n\n[34.17] PETCO Animal Supplies, Inc.\n\n[34.18] Leonard Green & Partners, L.P. and Texas Pacific Group\n\n[34.19] July 2006\n\n[34.20] Michaels Stores, Inc.\n\n[34.21] Bain Capital Partners LLC and The Blackstone Group\n\n[34.22] June 2006\n\n[34.23] The Sports Authority, Inc.\n\n[34.24] Leonard Green & Partners, L.P. and The Sports Authority Senior Management\n\n[34.25] January 2006\n\n[34.26] Linens N Things Inc.\n\n[34.27] Apollo Management LP\n\n[34.28] November 2005\n\n[34.29] Toys “R” Us, Inc.\n\n[34.30] Kohlberg Kravis Roberts & Co. L.P., Bain Capital Partners, LLC, and Vornado Realty Trust\n\n[34.31] March 2005\n\n[34.32] Using publicly available information, J.P. Morgan calculated, for each selected transaction, the ratio of the transaction value to the target company’s EBITDA for the latest publicly available twelve-month period immediately prior to announcement of the applicable transaction (“TV/LTM EBITDA”).\n\n[34.33] The following table presents the results of this analysis:\n\n[34.34] TV/LTM EBITDA\n\n[34.35] High\n\n[34.36] Low\n\n[34.37] Mean\n\n[34.38] Median\n\n[34.39] High\n\n[34.40] Low\n\n[34.41] Mean\n\n[34.42] Median\n\n[34.43] Based on the results of this analysis and taking into account differences in the Company’s business and such other factors as J.P. Morgan deemed appropriate, J.P. Morgan selected a multiple reference range of 8.5x – 11.0x for TV/LTM EBITDA and applied it to the Company’s estimated Adjusted EBITDA as of January 31, 2015 as provided by Company management. The analysis indicated an implied per share equity value range for shares of the Company’s common stock, rounded to the nearest $0.25, of between $70.50 and $91.50 per share, compared to the merger consideration of  $83.00 per share for shares of the Company’s common stock, the Company’s closing share price of  $78.82 on December 9, 2014, and the Company’s closing share price of  $59.81 on July 2, 2014.\n\n[34.44] Discounted Cash Flow Analysis\n\n[34.45] J.P. Morgan conducted a discounted cash flow analysis for the purpose of determining an implied fully diluted equity value per share for shares of the Company’s common stock. A discounted cash flow analysis is a method of evaluating an asset using estimates of the future unlevered free cash flows generated by the asset and taking into consideration the time value of money with respect to those cash flows by calculating their “present value.” The “unlevered free cash flows” refers to a calculation of the future cash flows\n\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"SIMPSON CTX page None idx 7 : Simpson Thacher and Bartlett LLP 425 Lexington Avenue New York, NY 10017 Facsimile: (212) 455-2502 Email: rsymons@stblaw.com Attention: Ryerson Symons\n\n[34.0] TABLE OF CONTENTS\n\n[34.1] 2005 – 2007 Transactions\n\n[34.2] Target\n\n[34.3] Buyer\n\n[34.4] Announcement Date\n\n[34.5] Claire’s Stores, Inc.\n\n[34.6] Apollo Management, L.P.\n\n[34.7] March 2007\n\n[34.8] Dollar General Corporation\n\n[34.9] Kohlberg Kravis Roberts & Co. L.P.\n\n[34.10] March 2007\n\n[34.11] GNC Parent Corporation\n\n[34.12] Ares Management LLC\n\n[34.13] February 2007\n\n[34.14] Guitar Center Inc.\n\n[34.15] Bain Capital Partners, LLC\n\n[34.16] June 2007\n\n[34.17] PETCO Animal Supplies, Inc.\n\n[34.18] Leonard Green & Partners, L.P. and Texas Pacific Group\n\n[34.19] July 2006\n\n[34.20] Michaels Stores, Inc.\n\n[34.21] Bain Capital Partners LLC and The Blackstone Group\n\n[34.22] June 2006\n\n[34.23] The Sports Authority, Inc.\n\n[34.24] Leonard Green & Partners, L.P. and The Sports Authority Senior Management\n\n[34.25] January 2006\n\n[34.26] Linens N Things Inc.\n\n[34.27] Apollo Management LP\n\n[34.28] November 2005\n\n[34.29] Toys “R” Us, Inc.\n\n[34.30] Kohlberg Kravis Roberts & Co. L.P., Bain Capital Partners, LLC, and Vornado Realty Trust\n\n[34.31] March 2005\n\n[34.32] Using publicly available information, J.P. Morgan calculated, for each selected transaction, the ratio of the transaction value to the target company’s EBITDA for the latest publicly available twelve-month period immediately prior to announcement of the applicable transaction (“TV/LTM EBITDA”).\n\n[34.33] The following table presents the results of this analysis:\n\n[34.34] TV/LTM EBITDA\n\n[34.35] High\n\n[34.36] Low\n\n[34.37] Mean\n\n[34.38] Median\n\n[34.39] High\n\n[34.40] Low\n\n[34.41] Mean\n\n[34.42] Median\n\n[34.43] Based on the results of this analysis and taking into account differences in the Company’s business and such other factors as J.P. Morgan deemed appropriate, J.P. Morgan selected a multiple reference range of 8.5x – 11.0x for TV/LTM EBITDA and applied it to the Company’s estimated Adjusted EBITDA as of January 31, 2015 as provided by Company management. The analysis indicated an implied per share equity value range for shares of the Company’s common stock, rounded to the nearest $0.25, of between $70.50 and $91.50 per share, compared to the merger consideration of  $83.00 per share for shares of the Company’s common stock, the Company’s closing share price of  $78.82 on December 9, 2014, and the Company’s closing share price of  $59.81 on July 2, 2014.\n\n[34.44] Discounted Cash Flow Analysis\n\n[34.45] J.P. Morgan conducted a discounted cash flow analysis for the purpose of determining an implied fully diluted equity value per share for shares of the Company’s common stock. A discounted cash flow analysis is a method of evaluating an asset using estimates of the future unlevered free cash flows generated by the asset and taking into consideration the time value of money with respect to those cash flows by calculating their “present value.” The “unlevered free cash flows” refers to a calculation of the future cash flows\n\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Command exited with code 0."}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /home/uctpiaj/work/work_tmp && python3 - <<'EOF'\\nimport json, re\\ndata=json.load(open('pages.json'))\\n# locate Simpson page\\nfor d in data:\\n    for j,t in enumerate(d['paras']):\\n        if 'Simpson' in t or 'Cravath' in t:\\n            print(\\\"SIMPSON CTX page\\\", d['page'], \\\"idx\\\", j, \\\":\\\", t[:1500])\\n            print()\\n# page 34 paragraphs\\nfor d in data:\\n    if d['page']=='34':\\n        for j,t in enumerate(d['paras']):\\n     