 who=\"2 unnamed financial submitters (cohort; indications below $80.00)\",\n355:     what=\"Bid\", process=1, round=1, type=\"Financial\",\n356:     terms=\"Two of the six submitters indicated prices below $80.00 per share; values not disclosed; not advanced to the final round (closed at R022). Count 2 = the two submitting units; no individual prices exist in the filing.\",\n357:     formality=\"Informal\", conditions=\"Heavy\",\n358:     why=IOI_WHY + \" Six parties submitted on 10/30 and only four “bidders that had indicated a price or range at or above $80.00” were allowed to proceed (p. 24), leaving two submitters below the threshold whose prices are not disclosed (p. 24).\",\n359:     source=\"P-021; P-022\", review=\"Q2\", count=2,\n360:     date_from=\"10/30/2014\", date_to=\"10/30/2014\", working=\"10/30/2014\",\n361:     date_basis=\"Reported day\", date_method=\"Reported\",\n362:     price_kind=\"Undisclosed\", all_cash=\"Not stated\", cond_detail=IOI_DETAIL, page=24,\n363:     related=\"R022 (dropped)\",\n364: ))\n365: \n366: # Inferred residual cohort (id R045; reading position #20.5; new unused identifier per instruction)\n367: rows.append(R(\n368:     row_id=\"R045\", num=20.5,\n369:     when=\"by 10/30/2014\",\n370:     who=\"9 unnamed financial NDA signers (cohort; no indication submitted)\",\n371:     what=\"Did not submit\", process=1, round=1, type=\"Financial\",\n372:     terms=\"Inferred: residual — 15 NDA signers − 6 submitters = 9 non-submitters; no indication of interest reported from these signers by the 10/30/2014 deadline. CLOSED by inference; no decision date, motive or voluntary withdrawal is inferred, and no individual rows are created for anonymous members.\",\n373:     why=\"Base and continuing set from the same passages: “In the first week of October 2014, the Company entered into confidentiality and standstill agreements with 15 potentially interested financial buyers” (p. 23); “On October 30, six of the potentially interested parties submitted indications of interest” (p. 24). Arithmetic 15 − 6 = 9. Base assumes every submitter was among the 15 signers and that the Buyer Group counts as one signer/unit (Q2).\",\n374:     source=\"P-018; P-021; P-022\", review=\"Q2; Q3\", count=9,\n375:     date_from=\"10/30/2014\", working=\"10/30/2014\",\n376:     date_basis=\"Relative only\", date_method=\"Assigned: deadline\",\n377:     decided_by=\"Unknown\", exit_reason=\"Not stated\", outcome_basis=\"Inferred: residual\", page=23,\n378:     related=\"R012 (base population); R015–R020 (submitters)\",\n379: ))\n380: \n381: # ---- Round 2 -----------------------------------------------------------------\n382: rows.append(R(\n383:     row_id=\"R021\", num=21,\n384:     when=\"11/03/2014\",\n385:     who=\"PetSmart board\",\n386:     what=\"Round opened\", process=1, round=2,\n387:     terms=\"Board selected the four bidders whose indications were at or above $80.00 per share (Buyer Group, Bidder 2 and two unnamed bidders) to proceed to the final round of the sale process. Purpose: final-round diligence, negotiation of definitive documentation and final bids; bidders were asked to submit comments on the circulated merger agreement with their final bids (R024). Final bids were initially planned for 12/05/2014 (communication date not disclosed), then revised to 12/10 and an improvement deadline of 12/12 (R027, R028, R033).\",\n388:     why=\"“The board determined to allow the four bidders that had indicated a price or range at or above $80.00 per share to proceed to the final round of the sale process” (p. 24). The filing calls this stage the final round and the later solicitation was for “final bids” and “best and final” offers (pp. 24–26).\",\n389:     source=\"P-022; P-025; P-026\", review=\"Q1\",\n390:     date_from=\"11/03/2014\", date_to=\"11/03/2014\", working=\"11/03/2014\",\n391:     date_basis=\"Reported day\", date_method=\"Reported\", page=24,\n392:     round_finality=\"Announced as final\",\n393:     related=\"R011 (prior round); R022; R027\",\n394: ))\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 395]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /home/uctpiaj/work/work_tmp/deal_data.py, lines 330-394\n330:     price_low=78.0, price_high=78.0, price_kind=\"Point\", price_origin=\"Stated\",\n331:     currency=\"USD\", all_cash=\"Not stated\", cash_close=78.0, cond_detail=IOI_DETAIL, page=24,\n332:     related=\"R019 (revises); R021\",\n333: ))\n334: \n335: rows.append(R(\n336:     row_id=\"R019\", num=19,\n337:     when=\"10/30–11/02/2014; day not disclosed\",\n338:     who=\"Bidder 2\",\n339:     what=\"Bid\", process=1, round=1, type=\"Financial\",\n340:     terms=\"Revised indication of $81.00–$84.00 per share after J.P. Morgan's 10/30–11/02 calls; first Bid row for this bidder in the round (R018) carries the Count.\",\n341:     formality=\"Informal\", conditions=\"Heavy\",\n342:     why=IOI_WHY + \" “As a result of its discussions with J.P. Morgan, another bidder (which we refer to as “Bidder 2”) … increased its indication to a range of $81.00 to $84.00 per share” (p. 24). Discussions ran 10/30–11/02; the revision day is not disclosed.\",\n343:     source=\"P-021\", review=\"Q6\", count=0,\n344:     date_from=\"10/30/2014\", date_to=\"11/02/2014\", working=\"11/01/2014\",\n345:     date_basis=\"Reported interval\", date_method=\"Assigned: midpoint\",\n346:     price_low=81.0, price_high=84.0, price_kind=\"Bidder range\", price_origin=\"Stated\",\n347:     currency=\"USD\", all_cash=\"Not stated\", cond_detail=IOI_DETAIL, page=24,\n348:     related=\"revises R018; R021\",\n349: ))\n350: \n351: rows.append(R(\n352:     row_id=\"R020\", num=20,\n353:     when=\"10/30/2014\",\n354:     who=\"2 unnamed financial submitters (cohort; indications below $80.00)\",\n355:     what=\"Bid\", process=1, round=1, type=\"Financial\",\n356:     terms=\"Two of the six submitters indicated prices below $80.00 per share; values not disclosed; not advanced to the final round (closed at R022). Count 2 = the two submitting units; no individual prices exist in the filing.\",\n357:     formality=\"Informal\", conditions=\"Heavy\",\n358:     why=IOI_WHY + \" Six parties submitted on 10/30 and only four “bidders that had indicated a price or range at or above $80.00” were allowed to proceed (p. 24), leaving two submitters below the threshold whose prices are not disclosed (p. 24).\",\n359:     source=\"P-021; P-022\", review=\"Q2\", count=2,\n360:     date_from=\"10/30/2014\", date_to=\"10/30/2014\", working=\"10/30/2014\",\n361:     date_basis=\"Reported day\", date_method=\"Reported\",\n362:     price_kind=\"Undisclosed\", all_cash=\"Not stated\", cond_detail=IOI_DETAIL, page=24,\n363:     related=\"R022 (dropped)\",\n364: ))\n365: \n366: # Inferred residual cohort (id R045; reading position #20.5; new unused identifier per instruction)\n367: rows.append(R(\n368:     row_id=\"R045\", num=20.5,\n369:     when=\"by 10/30/2014\",\n370:     who=\"9 unnamed financial NDA signers (cohort; no indication submitted)\",\n371:     what=\"Did not submit\", process=1, round=1, type=\"Financial\",\n372:     terms=\"Inferred: residual — 15 NDA signers − 6 submitters = 9 non-submitters; no indication of interest reported from these signers by the 10/30/2014 deadline. CLOSED by inference; no decision date, motive or voluntary withdrawal is inferred, and no individual rows are created for anonymous members.\",\n373:     why=\"Base and continuing set from the same passages: “In the first week of October 2014, the Company entered into confidentiality and standstill agreements with 15 potentially interested financial buyers” (p. 23); “On October 30, six of the potentially interested parties submitted indications of interest” (p. 24). Arithmetic 15 − 6 = 9. Base assumes every submitter was among the 15 signers and that the Buyer Group counts as one signer/unit (Q2).\",\n374:     source=\"P-018; P-021; P-022\", review=\"Q2; Q3\", count=9,\n375:     date_from=\"10/30/2014\", working=\"10/30/2014\",\n376:     date_basis=\"Relative only\", date_method=\"Assigned: deadline\",\n377:     decided_by=\"Unknown\", exit_reason=\"Not stated\", outcome_basis=\"Inferred: residual\", page=23,\n378:     related=\"R012 (base population); R015–R020 (submitters)\",\n379: ))\n380: \n381: # ---- Round 2 -----------------------------------------------------------------\n382: rows.append(R(\n383:     row_id=\"R021\", num=21,\n384:     when=\"11/03/2014\",\n385:     who=\"PetSmart board\",\n386:     what=\"Round opened\", process=1, round=2,\n387:     terms=\"Board selected the four bidders whose indications were at or above $80.00 per share (Buyer Group, Bidder 2 and two unnamed bidders) to proceed to the final round of the sale process. Purpose: final-round diligence, negotiation of definitive documentation and final bids; bidders were asked to submit comments on the circulated merger agreement with their final bids (R024). Final bids were initially planned for 12/05/2014 (communication date not disclosed), then revised to 12/10 and an improvement deadline of 12/12 (R027, R028, R033).\",\n388:     why=\"“The board determined to allow the four bidders that had indicated a price or range at or above $80.00 per share to proceed to the final round of the sale process” (p. 24). The filing calls this stage the final round and the later solicitation was for “final bids” and “best and final” offers (pp. 24–26).\",\n389:     source=\"P-022; P-025; P-026\", review=\"Q1\",\n390:     date_from=\"11/03/2014\", date_to=\"11/03/2014\", working=\"11/03/2014\",\n391:     date_basis=\"Reported day\", date_method=\"Reported\", page=24,\n392:     round_finality=\"Announced as final\",\n393:     related=\"R011 (prior round); R022; R027\",\n394: ))\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 395]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"limit\": 65, \"o