{"type":"text","timestamp":1789825355324,"sessionID":"ses_f462b66afffeUYg2nY8b6hqAEy","part":{"id":"prt_0b9e75dc5001TA00Cpq651AdOV_text-0","sessionID":"ses_f462b66afffeUYg2nY8b6hqAEy","messageID":"msg_0b9e75dc5001TA00Cpq651AdOV","type":"text","text":"The workbook is complete and all mechanical checks pass. Here is the delivery.\n\n## Deliverable\n\n**`extraction/petsmart.xlsx`** — four visible sheets plus the two hidden support sheets:\n\n| Sheet | Content |\n|---|---|\n| **Deal ledger** | 45 chronological rows (R001–R045), 14 readable columns + collapsed expandable field groups (Row id/Include, Count, dates, price, cash, Conditions detail, due date/treatment/finality, outcome fields, Page, Related rows, Deal). Filters, frozen headers, 15 drop-down-validated columns. |\n| **Summary** | Status, commercial account, deal facts, process/round map, participants and advisers, counts/auction screen (with live SUMIFS formulas), comparability and glossary. |\n| **Questions** | 8 grouped review items with recommendations and consequences, followed by the section 13 check results. |\n| **Source text** | P-001–P-040: the filing's background (pp. 21–26) plus opening reasons passages, in source order; X-001–X-040: every additional passage, table and annex text used. Ledger Source cells link internally to these rows. |\n| Hidden **Lists** / **AI original** | Exact controlled-category strings; values-only baseline copy of the delivered ledger (0 differences), used by the red-bold change-highlight rules (match by Row id and column). |\n\n## The sale in brief\n\nPetSmart, pushed by JANA's 9.9% 13D (07/03/2014) and Longview's public sale advocacy (07/07/2014), decided on 08/13/2014 to explore strategic alternatives, announced it 08/19/2014 and retained J.P. Morgan (engagement letter effective 08/21/2014). Twenty-seven parties contacted J.P. Morgan (24 financial, 3 strategic); 15 financial buyers signed confidentiality/standstill agreements in the first week of October and six submitted non-binding indications by 10/30 (Buyer Group $81–83, one $80–85, one \"≥$80\", Bidder 2 $78→$81–84, two below $80). On 11/03 the board advanced the four bidders at or above $80 into a final round; two unnamed finalists were authorized to combine as \"Bidder 3\". Final bids on 12/10 were $80.70 (Buyer Group) and $80.35 (Bidder 2); Bidder 3 dropped out rather than bid (valuation not above ~$78). Asked to improve, Bidder 2 submitted a best-and-final $81.50 and the Buyer Group moved from an oral $82.50 to a best-and-final $83.00 on 12/12. The board approved the Buyer Group's all-cash $83.00 offer on 12/13; the merger agreement, Longview rollover (3,012,050 shares ≈ $250m) and voting agreement (7,424,591 shares ≈ 7.5%) were signed and announced 12/14/2014. No competing proposal had appeared by the 02/02/2015 proxy date; closing (expected 1H 2015) is not observed in the filing.\n\n## Most consequential review items (recommendations in Q1–Q8)\n\n1. **Round map (Q1)** — one process; R1 anchored at the NDA wave (first week of October), not the 08/13 decision, 08/19 announcement, 10/03 meeting or inbound contact wave (all kept as rows); R2 = the final round from 11/03, Announced as final; the 12/05→12/10→12/12 changes are deadline revisions, not new rounds.\n2. **Counts (Q2)** — ledger uses six submitting units and the 15-signer base; the filing's \"5 bidder groups\" conflict and the Buyer-Group-as-one-unit assumption are preserved, not resolved.\n3. **Inferred closings (Q3)** — 9 non-submitters at the 10/30 deadline; two eliminated submitters; Bidder 3's exit; Bidder 2 not selected at signing. The likely mapping of unnamed bidders 1/2 to the Bidder 3 members stays a flagged hypothesis.\n4. **Classifications (Q4, Q6)** — Round-1 indications are Informal/Heavy-by-context (alternative: Insufficient evidence flagged); final bids Formal/Light; Bidder 3's communication is a valuation, not a priced bid; the ≥$80 bound wording is flagged.\n5. **Deadlines (Q5)** — 10/30 Enforced, 12/05 Extended (superseded), 12/10 Extended, 12/12 Enforced; no late acceptance; no exclusivity.\n\n## Checks\n\nPassed: coverage, participation continuity, dates/order, structure/tags, evidence (every quoted segment verified against the filing text). **Qualified:** counts (source conflict preserved), offers/classification (context-based conditions, bound ambiguity), workbook operation (see limitation). **Not run:** no spreadsheet-application test — LibreOffice is incomplete in this environment (`/usr/lib/libreoffice/share/registry/main.xcd` missing), so the SUMIFS formulas, internal hyperlinks, validations and change-highlight rules were verified structurally in the saved file and by independent Python recomputation (15/6/9/2/2), not by opening Excel/LibreOffice. No changed-cell highlights exist at delivery.","time":{"start":1789825342925,"end":1789825355324}}}
